- Used by the height graph: no

## Feature summary (web, SideFX reference)

- Source: https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/dilateerode.html
- Summary (EN): Expands or shrinks a layer, mostly to grow or trim masks. Positive radius dilates, negative radius erodes. Output is named dilate.
- Résumé (FR) : Élargit ou réduit une couche, en pratique pour agrandir ou rogner un masque.

- Inputs meaning: ["source: original layer to dilate or erode", "radius: optional per-pixel radius scaled by the Radius parameter", "mask: optional per-pixel mask scaled by the Mask parameter"]

- Key parameters: ["Signature: layer type accepted by the source", "Mask: mix of new value with original; default 1 uses only the new value", "Units: Image, Pixels or Local space for the radius", "Radius: dilation amount; positive dilates, negative erodes; clamped by the maximum", "Soft Edge: gradient for softer edges", "Fill Holes / Remove Specks: dilates inward to patch holes", "Maximum Pixel Radius: caps Radius to limit cost"]

- Caveats: ["Large radius values slow performance, which is why the clamp exists.", "The page is inconsistent on the clamp name: Maximum Pixel Radius in the parameter list, Maximum Radius in the Radius entry; check the label in your Houdini version."]

